[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585737604","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113216#issuecomment-3585737604","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113216","id":3585737604,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VugOE","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T12:59:34Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T12:59:34Z","body":"It seems both `ZSTD_getParams` and `ZSTD_findDecompressedSize` are part of zstd's \"advanced API\", which requires that you build with `ZSTD_STATIC_LINKING_ONLY`, which obviously can't be done with the system-provided dynamic library.\n\nI should be able to replace `ZSTD_findDecompressedSize` with `ZSTD_getFrameContentSize`, which for whatever reason is not part of the advanced API, and hopefully replacing `ZSTD_getParams` with things like `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter` will have the same effect as `ZSTD_getParams`, by inferring the compression parameters based on the compression level and source/dictionary size.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issue